# PARTE A (English version)

## A.1 What "the Software" is
"the Software" means the contents of this repository: source code, interfaces, texts, skills, prompts,
documentation, configurations, images and diagrams owned by Universalis Produzioni. Third-party components
included in or depended upon by the Software (libraries, models, fonts, icons) are **not** part of the
Software and remain under their own licenses (see A.8).

## A.2 Permitted uses with no written agreement
Every natural person is granted, free of charge and without contacting the licensor:

1. **personal, individual use** of the Software with no commercial purpose: study, experimentation, learning,
   evaluation, technical testing, personal and hobby projects;
2. **public demonstration** of the Software running (events, videos, presentations, articles, posts, lessons),
   provided it is free of charge and access to it is not sold or bundled into a paid offering;
3. **configuration** for one's own use: editing settings, prompts, skills and your own data, and using the
   Software's interfaces and APIs, does **not** constitute "making changes" under Part B.

## A.3 Mandatory attribution (condition of the license)
Whenever the Software is **used in public**, shown, demonstrated or mentioned in any material (video, slides,
posts, articles, websites, repositories, lessons, promotional messages), or **produces a work or content**
that is published or distributed, it must display, visibly and legibly, **both** the name
**"Universalis Harness"** and the link **https://github.com/Simus100/universalis-harness**.

In the Software's (or derived work's) interface the ownership notice must remain **visible and not
removable**. Removing, obscuring or replacing ownership notices is prohibited. **Strictly private** use (no
publication, no audience) does not require public display of the credit but remains subject to all other terms.

## A.4 Prohibited uses
Without a written agreement with Universalis Produzioni you may **not**:

1. **sell**, rent, license or sublicense the Software, or grant its use to third parties, for payment or free
   of charge;
2. **distribute** copies of the Software, even free of charge, even modified, even in part, including as part
   of another product, package, image, repository or distribution;
3. **offer the Software as a service** to third parties: hosting, SaaS, subscription, remote access, support
   based on the Software;
4. use the Software **in a business, professional or paid activity**, or on behalf of third parties for
   consideration, or in any way that yields a direct or indirect economic advantage (advertising, fundraising,
   training models intended for a product, etc.);
5. **present the Software as your own** or attribute it to anyone other than the licensor, claim ownership you
   do not have, or remove/alter copyright and license notices;
6. use the names **"Universalis"** and **"Universalis Harness"**, the logo and the visual identity (see A.7);
7. circumvent the above through intermediaries, nominees, forks, partial rewrites or code reorganization.

## A.5 Trial instances and testers
If the licensor granted you access to a **hosted instance** of the Software (for example as a tester or
demonstrator), that access is governed by the separate agreement you accepted with the licensor, not by this
license. This license covers the **code**, not the service. Credentials and accesses you receive are personal,
non-transferable, and do not allow you to let third parties use the instance.

## A.6 Changes
Changes to the code, the creation of derivative works, and their publication or distribution are not granted
by this license (Part B). The licensor may grant them in writing. Changes offered to the licensor via pull
requests are deemed offered on the terms stated in the repository's `CONTRIBUTING` file.

## A.7 Trademarks
This license grants **copyright** rights, not **trademark** rights. "Universalis" and "Universalis Harness" and
their graphic marks belong to the licensor. They may not be used to name, promote or label products, services
or forks, nor in any way that creates confusion about origin or suggests a non-existent affiliation.

## A.8 Third-party components
Third-party libraries, models, fonts, icons and other components keep their own licenses and notices even when
present in this repository: this license does **not** cover them and does **not** relicense them. In case of
conflict, the third party's license prevails for that component.

## A.9 No warranty and limitation of liability
The Software is provided **"as is"**, without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including
merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, freedom from defects and non-infringement. The licensor is
not liable for direct or indirect damages, loss of data, profit or opportunity arising from the use of, or
inability to use, the Software. Use is at your own risk.

## A.10 Breach and remedies
Any use not covered by this license is **unauthorized** and infringes copyright. Upon breach the licensor may
revoke all grants with immediate effect. If you receive a written notice of breach, your grants may continue
**only** if within **32 days** of receipt you cure the breach, remove unauthorized copies and correct it in a
